<h1>How to edit this site</h1>
<p class="lead">You change the site with <strong>Pages CMS</strong>, a free editing website. You fill in simple forms; the site updates itself about a minute after you press Save.</p>
<p><a class="btn" href="https://app.pagescms.org/" rel="noopener">Open the editor</a></p>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Sign in.</strong> Click “Open the editor”, type your email address, and click the sign-in link it emails you.</li>
  <li><strong>Pick “Items for sale”.</strong> You will see every item with its name, price and status.</li>
  <li><strong>Mark something sold.</strong> Click the item, change <em>Status</em> to <em>Sold</em> (or <em>On Hold</em>), then click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Change a price or words.</strong> Click the item, type in the box, then click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Add a new item.</strong> Click <strong>Add an entry</strong>, type a name, pick a category, add a price, upload photos from your computer or phone, then click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Items that need a quick check.</strong> Some items have a note in the <em>Please check</em> box, right under the name (you can also see it in the list, or type a word into the search). Fix what it says, for example add a photo or a price, then delete the note and click <strong>Save</strong>. Visitors never see these notes.</li>
  <li><strong>Your contact details and the welcome text</strong> are under “Site settings”. Your About page is under “About &amp; Contact page”.</li>
</ol>
<p>Don’t worry about mistakes: every change is saved as a new version, so Winston can always undo it.</p>
